# Led Astray's Mhasbaf against Arts and Crafts' 510 (a Progress, while its Prog bit 1 is clear: a GM clears it after
# each talk): a level 75 Warrior in Whitegate. Mhasbaf has no script, so a lone event always plays. Led Astray
# available (808, a Progress: a tie with 510), then accepted at Prog 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 (834, an Event, once per zone, plain
# at Prog 3: 510 wins every time). Rubahah (a script: his shop) at Prog 2: 811 is a Progress, so it plays every talk (a
# GM clears the Stage after each); an Event would alternate with the shop.
lists AhtUrhganWhitegate/Mhasbaf/onTrigger AhtUrhganWhitegate/Rubahah/onTrigger AhtUrhganWhitegate/onEventFinish/808 AhtUrhganWhitegate/onEventFinish/510 AhtUrhganWhitegate/onEventFinish/811
char zone=AhtUrhganWhitegate pos=56.2,-6,11.387 job=WAR lvl=75
quest AhtUrhgan.ArtsAndCrafts accepted
charvar Quest[6][1]Prog 0
login
trigger Mhasbaf                         # Led Astray available: 808 and 510 tie
finish option=0
